   "source": {
    "label": "thm:reg_icat",
    "number": "Theorem (thm:reg_icat)",
    "quote": "Let $T \\geq 1$. The sleeping regret incurred by \\algicat\\, (Alg.~\\ref{alg:icat}) can be bounded as:\n\\begin{eqnarray*}\nR_T & = & \\max_{\\pi: 2^{[K]} \\mapsto [K]}\\E\\bigg[ \\sum_{t=1}^{T}\\ell(i_t) - \\sum_{t=1}^{T}\\ell(\\pi(S_t)) \\bigg] \\\\\n& \\le & 16 K^{2} \\sqrt{ T \\ln T}  + 1 \\,,\n\\end{eqnarray*}\nfor the parameter choices $\\eta  =  \\sqrt{(\\log K)/(KT)}$,  $\\delta  =  K/T^2$, and \n\\[\n\\lambda_t  = \\min\\left\\{  2 K \\sqrt{\\frac{2\\log(K/\\delta)}{t}} + \\frac{8K\\log(K/\\delta)}{3t},1\\right\\} \\,.\n\\]"
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Regret is max over policies outside expectation over availabilities and learner randomness, against oblivious losses; recorded as pseudo_regret. Computing bar q_t needs O(2^K) per round, hence compute exponential."
  },
